-- The Shop tab is back on the website (it stays out of the apps), so its Help Center article comes back (migration 0282 had removed it).
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO help_articles (slug, title, category, kind, summary, body, keywords, video, sort, status, updated_by) VALUES ('what-is-the-shop-tab', 'What is the Shop tab?', 'find', 'answer', 'The Shop tab has seasonal ideas for lights and decorations. Each card opens an Amazon search, and we may earn a small commission at no cost to you.', 'The **Shop** tab is next to **Places** and **Favorites** on the map. On a phone it is in the bar at the bottom. It has ideas for each season, such as lights and decorations.

1. Open the map and tap **Shop**.
2. Tap the season button at the top of the list (it says **Shop for** and the season) to see ideas for another season.
3. Tap a card. It opens an Amazon search in a new tab.

- SoCal Lights does not sell anything. Buying happens on Amazon.
- The cards are affiliate links. As an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases, at no extra cost to you. The tab says so under the cards.
- Shop links never affect a contest, a listing or the order of the map list. The map, search, routes, voting and entering stay free.
- The Shop tab is on the website. It is not inside the SoCal Lights app.

See also [Is SoCal Lights free?](/help/is-it-free) and the [Privacy Policy](/privacy).', 'shop, shop tab, amazon, affiliate, buy lights, decorations, gift ideas, commission, associate, store', '', 160, 'published', 'seed');
